# Review: Composer

Every item in this spec is an app-level `test`, so each is judged on whether a Playwright spec in
`packages/e2e/composer-e2e` runs it, not on the app code. The multi-peer journeys are the solid part:
QA-7, QA-8, QA-9, QA-10 and QA-12 each have e2e tests, tagged with the QA id, that drive every step.
QA-5 and QA-6 are covered across several small tests. The single-user basics are thinner than their
`automated:` lists suggest: QA-1, QA-2 and QA-3 each have tests for a few steps but not the journey
(no multi-document deletion and survival, no document rename, no resolve and reopen). QA-4 is
diverged: the only test sends a prompt to a standalone Chat, not a document's companion assistant.
QA-11, QA-13 and QA-14 are run only by autocue recording scripts and the agent QA runner, which do not
count as automated tests.

Of 14 items: 7 done, 0 untested, 3 partial, 1 diverged, 3 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict QA-1: Only the create-space and create-document steps are automated; deletion and survival are not.
  status: partial
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/e2e/composer-e2e/src/playwright/basic.spec.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/e2e/composer-e2e/src/playwright/collections.spec.ts]
  note: |
    `basic.spec.ts` "create document" creates a space and one document; `collections.spec.ts` "create collection"
    creates a collection. No test creates three documents, deletes one from the navtree with the toast and error
    check, or verifies that the other two survive a reload.
```

```mdl
verdict QA-2: Workspace reorder and delete-undo are automated; rename and space switching are not.
  status: partial
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/e2e/composer-e2e/src/playwright/basic.spec.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/e2e/composer-e2e/src/playwright/collections.spec.ts]
  note: |
    "re-order workspaces" drags the rail and checks the order across a reload; "deletion undo restores collection"
    deletes and undoes a collection, not a document. No test renames a document, checks the restored plank reopens,
    or switches between two spaces and back.
```

```mdl
verdict QA-3: Create, reply, delete message and delete thread are automated; resolve and reopen are not.
  status: partial
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/e2e/composer-e2e/src/playwright/comments.spec.ts]
  note: |
    `comments.spec.ts` creates a comment, adds a second message, deletes a message and deletes a thread (plus edit,
    undo and selection, which the spec does not ask for). No test clicks Resolve or reopens a resolved thread.
```

```mdl
verdict QA-4: The only test chats with a standalone Chat object; nothing has the document assistant edit a document.
  status: diverged
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/e2e/composer-e2e/src/playwright/chat.spec.ts]
  note: |
    `chat.spec.ts` "sends a message and receives a response" creates a Chat, sends a prompt and waits for a reply.
    It does not open a document's companion assistant or check that a paragraph was translated in place.
```

```mdl
